**Lemma 5.4 (finite local checker and elimination of a general graph store).**
Given the actual public descriptions, a canonical pre-row record, its
constructor map and a T record, finite word instructions check exactly the
canonical patch record, obtain the native successor, and update the map.
Iterating this procedure from the foundation gives the same incidence
endpoint as executing its checked patches. A separate arbitrary seven-slot
graph interpreter is unnecessary on this domain.

Proof. Step has the supplied finite local cases of Definition 5.1. Its
finite effect list names only bounded local markers/slots, never a runtime
address. Definition 5.2 uses exactly those role/alias cases and UAS's
ordered templates. Find/Replace on finite words construct all eleven
fields; Equal checks them, including unchanged assignments and repeated
probes. The constructor map update gives exactly the fresh roles and
retains existing identities. UAS Theorem 2.4's local row square therefore
gives the same linked carrier for the successor. Induction over checked
records establishes the assertion. No arbitrary input graph or noncanonical
patch is assigned a successful native erasure by this lemma. ∎

